<<~ kanawai "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/ref/RFC-2119">>

<<~ ahu #/entry>>
! Fetch testimony; do not fetch certainty

The projection loom MAY acquire separately licensed source files through their
publisher's permitted routes, pin reviewed source bytes, compile authored
OpenSCAD references, and sample meshes as external testimony. A PR runner may
execute CAD and synthetic image tests without acquiring any third-party asset.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/contract>>
!! Source identity and build reproducibility

* ''An URL does not pin content.'' A bootstrap fetch yields an unreviewed
  SHA-256 and license receipt. An operator MAY inspect and commit a lock. Future
  runs MUST reject differing bytes unless explicitly reviewed and relocked.
* ''Provider boundaries govern access.'' Public CC0 OpenGameArt files use
  ordinary HTTPS. The modern Ur Sketchfab model requires its official Download
  API with user OAuth, or an official browser download. No viewer scraping,
  token logged in receipts, or secrets in untrusted pull-request workflows.
* ''Sources remain separate from inference.'' Archive contents and compiled
  OpenSCAD STL meshes enter a surface-witness adaptor with explicit native
  model units; no source can claim exact CAD union or measured archaeological
  alignment absent independent registration.
* ''Bound the work.'' External ZIPs face size, expansion, file-count,
  path-traversal and unexpected-file checks. GitHub Actions uses read-only
  repository permissions, bounded job time, recorded dependency versions,
  and produces short-lived preview and test artifacts.
* ''Local parity.'' The same Python scripts drive desktop/WSL use and CI;
  `references.lock.json` travels with the project when reviewed. CI success
  means tests passed, never that absent third-party sources became available.

<<~/ahu>>

